jim@XN.LL.MIT.EDU (Jim Washburn) writes:
>	I have a problem with 3 new games that have been posted.
>Nethack3.0, Galatic Bloodshed and Conquor.  When I try and make
>these games I always end up with the following messages:

>	Make: must be a seperator on rules line xxxx

>There appears to be (upon inspection of line xxx and those around
>it) nothing wrong.  Does anybody have a clue to what the problem
>is.  I have examined the make files for games which I have gotten
>installed successfully like Nethack2.3 and Omega and there are
>major differences in how each file is written.  Not being a C/Unix
>person I am unable to see why one works but the other doesn't.
>Any help would be appreciated.


I ran into this problem whenever I tried to install any software on
my 3b2s -- you'll need to go into the Makefile and change the spaces
to a tab, as in:

target:<sp><sp><sp><sp>depnd.h depnc.c
target:<tab>depnd.h depnc.c

(at least, I think that's what I had to do. maybe it was change tabs
to spaces...)

